6057934.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136057934.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Youth Congress workers caused a commotion at the Meta office in Hyderabad, protesting account suspensions affecting their leaders. This vandalism was denounced by leaders from both the BJP and BRS, who claimed it jeopardized the city's business-friendly image. N Ramchander Rao, president of Telangana BJP, criticized Congress for promoting such destructive behavior. Meanwhile, K T Rama Rao of BRS articulated that such incidents erode trust in companies like Meta.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/goondaism-isnt-a-bug-bjp-brs-attack-congress-over-meta-office-vandalism/articleshow/136057934.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/goondaism-isnt-a-bug-bjp-brs-attack-congress-over-meta-office-vandalism/articleshow/136057934.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T21:04:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136057996,imgsize-136454.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Modi ji should apologise': Congress alleges PM's Lucknow event led to cancellation of four weddings]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/modi-ji-should-apologise-congress-alleges-pms-lucknow-event-led-to-cancellation-of-four-weddings/articleshow/136057843.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136057843.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/modi-ji-should-apologise-congress-alleges-pms-lucknow-event-led-to-cancellation-of-four-weddings/articleshow/136057843.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/modi-ji-should-apologise-congress-alleges-pms-lucknow-event-led-to-cancellation-of-four-weddings/articleshow/136057843.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T21:00:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136057926,imgsize-1492411.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[N-safety regulator AERB grants criticality nod to Rajasthan’s N-plant unit-8, reactor moves closer to power generation]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/n-safety-regulator-aerb-grants-criticality-nod-to-rajasthans-n-plant-unit-8-reactor-moves-closer-to-power-generation/articleshow/136057720.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136057720.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/n-safety-regulator-aerb-grants-criticality-nod-to-rajasthans-n-plant-unit-8-reactor-moves-closer-to-power-generation/articleshow/136057720.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/n-safety-regulator-aerb-grants-criticality-nod-to-rajasthans-n-plant-unit-8-reactor-moves-closer-to-power-generation/articleshow/136057720.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T20:51:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Surendra Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136057778,imgsize-70244.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Working to suppress India’s rise': US panel report flags China's support to Pakistan during Operation Sindoor]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/working-to-suppress-indias-rise-us-panel-report-flags-chinas-support-to-pakistan-during-operation-sindoor/articleshow/136056716.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136056716.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In May 2025, China's military support for Pakistan intensified India's security dilemmas. This report reveals Beijing's ongoing strategies aimed at stifling India's strategic advancements through both military and economic tactics. With Pakistan receiving advanced weaponry, India's concerns over a dual-threat scenario have been amplified. The evolving military alliance between China and Pakistan poses greater risks for India moving forward, showcasing a troubling shift in regional security dynamics.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/working-to-suppress-indias-rise-us-panel-report-flags-chinas-support-to-pakistan-during-operation-sindoor/articleshow/136056716.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/working-to-suppress-indias-rise-us-panel-report-flags-chinas-support-to-pakistan-during-operation-sindoor/articleshow/136056716.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T20:10:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136056960,imgsize-49526.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['When you promote rakshasas': BJP MP Nishikant Dubey takes swipe at Meta amid youth Congress protests]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/when-you-promote-rakshasas-bjp-mp-nishikant-dubey-takes-swipe-at-meta-amid-youth-congress-protests/articleshow/136056344.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136056344.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/when-you-promote-rakshasas-bjp-mp-nishikant-dubey-takes-swipe-at-meta-amid-youth-congress-protests/articleshow/136056344.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/when-you-promote-rakshasas-bjp-mp-nishikant-dubey-takes-swipe-at-meta-amid-youth-congress-protests/articleshow/136056344.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T19:44:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136056408,imgsize-104474.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Country's character remains the same': PM Modi praises people for heeding call to not buy gold]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/countrys-character-remains-the-same-pm-modi-praises-people-for-heeding-call-to-not-buy-gold/articleshow/136056082.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136056082.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/countrys-character-remains-the-same-pm-modi-praises-people-for-heeding-call-to-not-buy-gold/articleshow/136056082.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/countrys-character-remains-the-same-pm-modi-praises-people-for-heeding-call-to-not-buy-gold/articleshow/136056082.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T19:36:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136056299,imgsize-77526.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MEA clears Taj Mahal visit for Pakistan delegation, no nod for Nizamuddin dargah]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mea-clears-taj-mahal-visit-for-pakistan-delegation-no-nod-for-nizamuddin-dargah/articleshow/136055919.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136055919.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A Pakistani delegation, led by Musadik Masood Malik, is in India for the SCO Civilisational Dialogue Forum. They have been permitted to visit the Taj Mahal, Humayun's Tomb, and Dilli Haat. However, their visit to Nizamuddin dargah has not been security cleared. This visit marks the first by a Pakistani minister to India in three years. The programme emphasizes shared civilizational heritage and cross-cultural engagement among SCO member countries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mea-clears-taj-mahal-visit-for-pakistan-delegation-no-nod-for-nizamuddin-dargah/articleshow/136055919.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mea-clears-taj-mahal-visit-for-pakistan-delegation-no-nod-for-nizamuddin-dargah/articleshow/136055919.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T19:25:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136055939,imgsize-38186.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['India not a rogue state': Wangchuk claims police deployment withdrawn after court hearing]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-not-a-rogue-state-wangchuk-cries-foul-over-house-arrest-says-police-pulled-out-after-court-order/articleshow/136055057.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136055057.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonam Wangchuk accused the Ladakh administration of effectively placing him under house arrest since November 11. He appealed to President Droupadi Murmu and Prime Minister Narendra Modi to uphold constitutional values. Wangchuk expressed concerns about government misuse of police for actions that compromise their duties. He opposed the timing of Hill Council elections, arguing that many residents would be unable to participate.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-not-a-rogue-state-wangchuk-cries-foul-over-house-arrest-says-police-pulled-out-after-court-order/articleshow/136055057.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-not-a-rogue-state-wangchuk-cries-foul-over-house-arrest-says-police-pulled-out-after-court-order/articleshow/136055057.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T19:13:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136055769,imgsize-147304.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Census-related delimitation should be put on hold for 25 years': CPM general secretary MA Baby]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/census-related-delimitation-should-be-put-on-hold-for-25-years-cpm-general-secretary-ma-baby/articleshow/136055191.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136055191.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/census-related-delimitation-should-be-put-on-hold-for-25-years-cpm-general-secretary-ma-baby/articleshow/136055191.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/census-related-delimitation-should-be-put-on-hold-for-25-years-cpm-general-secretary-ma-baby/articleshow/136055191.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-21T19:06:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136055605,imgsize-73586.cms"/></item></channel></rss>